{
 "note": "R45 \u2014 NHL 11 / 12 `CTX0` v3.1 condition / expression script ids joined to the `.gas` (`CSIS`) blob header id words (read-only).\n\nOn v4.5 (NHL 13\u2013Legacy) every `.gas` blob begins with `u32 id == its ordinal k`, so a context's blob reference is an index (2026-09-20 r22,\n2026-09-21 handoff 01). On v3.1 the ids in the context records exceed the blob count (handoff 16), so the index rule cannot hold. This probe\nreads every `.gas` blob header (`u32 id | w1 w2 w3 | ptr | ...`) of the NHL 11 / 12 sets, builds `id word -> blob ordinal` and joins:\n  * every condition's script id (record -> conditions[].blob) and every expression parameter's script id (item params kind 1),\n  * both directions: context ids without a blob (unresolved references, kept in full) and blobs no context references,\n  * whether the id-word map is injective, whether the ordinal order correlates with the id, and whether blob w1..w3 / ptr shapes\n    distinguish condition blobs from parameter blobs (as the v4.5 disjointness did).\nNothing is assumed from v4.5; unresolved references are listed, not dropped. Trees: X360 NHL 11, PS3 NHL 11, X360 NHL 12 (loose\n`audio/context`); sets `pbp_eng` and `crowds`.\nUsage: python r45_ctx0_v31_script_ids_vs_gas.py <out.json>\n",
